Package: hunmin
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fcitx5
Recommends: hunmin-en-us
Description: Korean input method engine (libhunmin core + fcitx5 addon)
 libhunmin is a portable Hangul input engine where keyboard layouts are
 data files rather than code. It matches libhangul behaviour for the
 standard layouts (golden-vector and parity tests) and implements
 신세벌식 P2 (sin3-p2) including symbol tiers, 초성체 and 옛한글 rules.
 .
 This package ships the shared library, the hunmin-sim trace simulator,
 the layout/compose data files, and the fcitx5 addon (addon and input
 method name "hunmin", coexisting with fcitx5-hangul).
 .
 The English word list used by the automatic Hangul/English switch ships
 as hunmin-en-us, and this package Recommends it, so a plain install has one
 dictionary and the feature can be used before a distribution mechanism for
 additional dictionaries exists (ruling 2026-11-01; SPEC-MODES R8-정정-2, B3).
 A machine without it is still a normal installation: the engine answers "no
 English words" and every mode keeps working.

Package: hunmin-en-us
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: hunspell en_US word list for hunmin's Hangul/English switch
 The English word set behind hunmin's automatic Hangul/English switch
 (SPEC-MODES R8-정정's english_valid). It is hunspell en_US expanded one
 affix level, lowercased and sorted, generated by tools/en-us2data.py and
 shipped as /usr/share/hunmin/modes/ next to its LICENCE and provenance.
 .
 It is a separate package on purpose: the ruling that created the feature
 makes its data a separate distribution, so that the switch can be enabled
 only where the data is present (B3). With this package absent, the engine
 answers "no English words" and every mode keeps working; see
 /usr/share/hunmin/modes/meta.json for the source, the method and what the
 list does not represent.
 .
 Licence: SCOWL's permission notice plus the hunspell .aff's BSD, both
 reproduced in full in /usr/share/hunmin/modes/LICENSE.md and in
 /usr/share/doc/hunmin-en-us/copyright.
